            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked what Google\u2019s definition of \u201cinteroperability\u201d was, noting it seemed one\u2011directional."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0ff88de86221334e2bd06763dfe399841d3b9d1e943b330f2e969f33c28d1b36",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0ff88de86221-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas asked whether the Court needed to decide more than the declaring code."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0ff88de86221334e2bd06763dfe399841d3b9d1e943b330f2e969f33c28d1b36",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0ff88de86221-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 68,
              "start": 68
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas later asked whether the Federal Circuit applied the proper review standard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0ff88de86221334e2bd06763dfe399841d3b9d1e943b330f2e969f33c28d1b36",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0ff88de86221-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether copyright protects computer programs but not methods of operation."
      }
    ],
